{"name":"Asparagus Sprig","hex":"#576f44","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"asparagus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various perennial plants of the genus Asparagus having leaflike stems, scalelike leaves, and small flowers.","The young shoots of Asparagus officinalis eaten as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asparagus"},{"term":"sprig","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small shoot or twig of a tree or other plant; a spray.","An ornament resembling a small shoot or twig."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate with sprigs, or with representations of sprigs, as in embroidery or pottery.","To nail the sole onto a shoe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sprig"}],"entries":[{"title":"Asparagus","blocks":[{"text":"Asparagus or garden asparagus is a perennial flowering plant species in the genus Asparagus native to Eurasia. Widely cultivated as a vegetable crop, its young shoots are used as a spring vegetable. In 2024, world production of asparagus was 8.9 million tonnes, led by China with 87% of the total."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asparagus","wikidata":"Q28367"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse","wikidata":"Q105563495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Asparagus-Bundle.jpg/500px-Asparagus-Bundle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Asparagus